# ArtiCode Academy — the jobs of the `backup` container (MOD-17-T04, D-R92).
#
# A template: at start the entrypoint replaces the two placeholders with
# BACKUP_SCHEDULE (default "30 2 * * *" — every night at 02:30) and
# BACKUP_DRILL_SCHEDULE (default "0 4 1 * *" — the 1st of every month at 04:00),
# checks them, and writes the result to /etc/cron.d/articode-backup (root, 0644).
# Times are in the container's TZ (default UTC). To change a time, set the
# variable in the academy's env file and recreate the container; to change the
# jobs themselves, edit this file and rebuild the image.
#
# Jobs start as root only to open the container's stdout/stderr (/proc/1/fd/*);
# each script re-executes itself as `postgres` before doing anything else.
SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin:/sbin:/bin
MAILTO=""

@BACKUP_SCHEDULE@ root /usr/local/bin/backup.sh >/proc/1/fd/1 2>/proc/1/fd/2
@BACKUP_DRILL_SCHEDULE@ root /usr/local/bin/restore-drill.sh >/proc/1/fd/1 2>/proc/1/fd/2
